Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.50,0:00:06.19,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Tabular language models could unlock the spreadsheets buried inside industrial companies,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:06.27,0:00:07.94,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}but they need labeled data,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:08.02,0:00:11.83,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and only scarce experts can annotate these technical tables.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:11.91,0:00:16.04,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Presented at NeurIPS 2022 by Ringsquandl and Koleva from Siemens,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:16.12,0:00:22.01,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}this paper asks: can active learning cut that labeling cost for sub-cell entity recognition?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:22.09,0:00:26.54,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Their headline finding is that a batch-diverse gradient method, BADGE,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:26.62,0:00:30.17,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}matches full-training performance with far fewer labels,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:30.25,0:00:33.61,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}while forcing maximum table diversity actually hurts.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:33.99,0:00:35.92,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Industry runs on spreadsheets.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:36.00,0:00:41.09,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Operators track equipment, sensors, and vessels in loosely structured tables,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:41.17,0:00:48.33,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and extracting that information automatically means fine-tuning tabular language models on labeled examples.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:48.41,0:00:53.64,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}But these tables use highly technical language only a few experts can annotate,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:53.72,0:00:55.78,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}so labeling gets expensive fast.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:55.86,0:00:59.74,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The paper frames this as sub-cell named entity recognition,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:59.82,0:01:02.42,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}a genuinely new active learning problem,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:02.50,0:01:06.45,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}since each cell carries multiple token-level labels at once.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:06.83,0:01:12.50,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Active learning is built for this setting: plentiful unlabeled data and expensive labels,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:12.58,0:01:15.93,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}squeezing the most performance from every annotation.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:16.01,0:01:19.88,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}But big transformer models can't learn one example at a time;
Dialogue: 0,0:01:19.96,0:01:22.59,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}they train in batches over several epochs,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:22.67,0:01:26.60,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}so the acquisition function must choose a whole batch at once.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:26.68,0:01:30.68,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Pure uncertainty sampling grabs very similar, correlated cells,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:30.76,0:01:33.39,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}often from the same table, wasting budget.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:33.47,0:01:37.79,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Yet no one had studied active learning with tabular language models,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:37.87,0:01:39.34,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}the gap this work fills.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:39.72,0:01:45.62,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The model is a tabular language model: a transformer encoder that swaps vanilla attention
Dialogue: 0,0:01:45.70,0:01:50.46,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}for a row-column visibility matrix with within-cell positional encoding,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:50.54,0:01:53.35,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}so every token is aware of the whole table.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:53.43,0:01:58.86,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}A decoder tags each token over four entity types: equipment tags, equipment names,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:58.94,0:02:00.95,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}physical quantities, and units.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:01.03,0:02:03.57,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}On top sits pool-based active learning,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:03.65,0:02:08.21,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}repeatedly picking the most informative cells for an expert to label.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:08.29,0:02:14.05,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Four acquisition functions compete: MNLP scores normalized log-probability uncertainty;
Dialogue: 0,0:02:14.13,0:02:17.08,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}MNLP-plus forces round-robin table diversity;
Dialogue: 0,0:02:17.16,0:02:22.52,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}BADGE clusters per-cell gradient embeddings with k-means-plus-plus for uncertain,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:22.60,0:02:25.48,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}diverse batches; and Rand samples uniformly.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:25.86,0:02:31.23,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Evaluation uses a real industrial dataset, not an academic benchmark.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:31.31,0:02:37.23,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Spreadsheets from several plants were downsampled to at most five rows each,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:37.31,0:02:43.08,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and expert annotators labeled every cell with the Prodigy span-based tool.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:43.16,0:02:47.74,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}A random split gives 55 training tables and 24 for testing.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:47.82,0:02:53.27,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The training set holds 4,774 cells but only about 1,100 entity labels,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:53.35,0:02:59.12,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}just 0.23 per cell, meaning roughly 77 percent of cells contain no entity,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:59.20,0:03:02.91,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}an extreme imbalance typical of industrial data.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:03.29,0:03:09.79,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Performance is micro-averaged F1 on the held-out test set across active learning iterations.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:09.87,0:03:17.95,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}BADGE is the standout: it beats random selection and even surpasses the ceiling from training on the full dataset,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:18.03,0:03:19.59,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}using far fewer labels.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:19.67,0:03:23.03,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Pure uncertainty sampling with MNLP disappoints,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:23.11,0:03:28.18,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}edging past random only after around 500 labels, and with high variance.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:28.26,0:03:34.19,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Most striking, MNLP-plus, which forces maximum table diversity, is the worst of all.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:34.57,0:03:38.62,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The four acquisition functions effectively ablate diversity,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:38.70,0:03:42.68,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and the lesson is that the right amount matters enormously.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:42.76,0:03:45.36,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}BADGE's built-in batch diversity helps,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:45.44,0:03:50.45,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}but MNLP-plus's forced maximum diversity hurts, falling below even random.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:50.53,0:03:57.34,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Tracking how many distinct tables each method draws from explains why: MNLP fixates on a few tables,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:57.42,0:04:02.36,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}MNLP-plus spreads across as many as possible, and BADGE lands in between.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:02.44,0:04:08.07,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The goal isn't maximum diversity but a careful trade-off with per-cell uncertainty.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:08.45,0:04:15.34,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The lasting message: active learning really can slash the expert-labeling cost of tabular language models,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:15.42,0:04:18.16,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}but only if diversity is handled with care.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:18.24,0:04:22.43,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Cell-level acquisition with built-in batch diversity, like BADGE,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:22.51,0:04:26.70,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}reaches full-training performance using a fraction of the labels,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:26.78,0:04:30.06,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}while bluntly maximizing table diversity backfires.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:30.14,0:04:34.79,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Balance diversity against uncertainty rather than maximize either alone.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:34.87,0:04:39.58,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}As the first work here, it flags two frontiers: acquisition compute cost,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:39.66,0:04:41.49,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and annotator cognitive load.
